{"body":"PR: https://github.com/Knowledge-Graph-Hub/kg-microbe/pull/1750\n\nThe first bounded official MediaDive SPARQL metadata request returned HTTP200 with recognized native counters (1,772,251 normal triples; six permutations), but an empty `name-index`. The discovery helper refused it because it required a nonempty index label. The official client accepts the empty label while displaying counters. This is a helper compatibility defect, not association evidence or dataset freshness.\n\nFix in scope: accept string names including empty, record `index_name_available=false` and `dataset_freshness_established=false`, and retain rejection of missing/nonstring names, error envelopes and invalid counters. Preserve the failed receipt unchanged. Add an offline regression and independently review the corrected helper.\n\nEvidence retained in `data/rebuild-evidence/20261105/mediadive-resolution-1734/`: `sparql-probes/stats-1/`, `unnamed-stats-assessment-1.json`, `sparql-probe-independent-review-3.json`. Corrected helper SHA256: d2d8761613401173c3bf63db83a29053ee1f48ee3abbef0c51aff3459c4e761d.\n","comments":[],"number":1760,"state":"OPEN","title":"MediaDive discovery: preserve unnamed official index metadata without claiming freshness","url":"https://github.com/Knowledge-Graph-Hub/kg-microbe/issues/1760"}
